0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93;">&nbsp;</p></di=
v><div class=3D""><div style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; =
font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93;" class=3D"">The good news is that we =
have found some English PDFs of SM2, including the missing part 1 and =
part 3. Will continue to find English translations of other SM standards =
mentioned in the draft.</div></div><div class=3D""><p class=3D"MsoNormal" =
style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: =
=E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93;">&nbsp;</p></div><div class=3D""><div style=3D"margin:=
 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93;" =
class=3D"">So, if we host a free website, say on Github or so, to =
provide those docs, is it convenient for you guys? Or should we just =
drop the &nbsp; PDF files to this mailing list as attachments?</div><div =
class=3D""><div style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; =
font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93;" class=3D""><br class=3D""><br =
class=3D""></div><div class=3D""><div style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; =
font-size: 12pt; font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93;" class=3D"">On Aug 16, =
2019, at 10:58 PM, Rene Struik &lt;<a =
href=3D"mailto:rstruik.ext@gmail.com" target=3D"_blank" style=3D"color: =
purple; text-decoration: underline;" =
class=3D"">rstruik.ext@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div></div><p =
class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; =
font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93;">&nbsp;</p><div class=3D""><div =
class=3D""><div class=3D""><div style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: =
12pt; font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93;" class=3D"">Arguably, "national" =
crypto specifications garnish more stature if these are made available =
to the pubic by that standard-setting body itself (who, thereby, acts as =
its authoritative source), without deference to a third party (that may, =
independently from the originator, enforce document control [e.g., by =
effectuating technical changes or enforcing controlled =
dissemination]).</div></div><div class=3D""><p class=3D"MsoNormal" =
style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: =
=E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93;">&nbsp;</p></div><div class=3D""><div style=3D"margin:=
 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93;" =
class=3D"">Since your draft introducing SM cipher suites with TLS1.3 =
appeals to the authority of a standard-setting authority, easy =
availability of the full and accredited technical documentation to the =
IETF community helps in scrutiny and, e.g., evaluating claims in the =
security considerations section.</div></div><div class=3D""><p =
class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; =
font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93;">&nbsp;</p></div><div class=3D""><div =
style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=
=93;" class=3D"">On 8/16/2019 3:06 AM, Kepeng Li wrote:</div></div><div =
class=3D""><div class=3D""><div class=3D""><div style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm =
0pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93; background-color: =
white;" class=3D""><span style=3D"font-size: 14px; font-family: Arial, =
sans-serif;" class=3D"">Hi Rene and all,</span></div></div></div><div =
class=3D""><div class=3D""><p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin: 0cm =
0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93; =
background-color: white; background-position: initial initial; =
background-repeat: initial initial;">&nbsp;</p></div></div><div =
class=3D""><div class=3D""><pre style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: =
12pt; font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93; line-height: 21px; =
background-color: white; background-position: initial initial; =
background-repeat: initial initial;" class=3D""><span style=3D"font-size: =
14px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);" =
class=3D"">&gt; Since the ISO documents are not available to the general =
</span></pre><pre style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; =
font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93; line-height: 21px; background-color: =
white; background-position: initial initial; background-repeat: initial =
initial;" class=3D""><span style=3D"font-size: 14px; font-family: Arial, =
sans-serif; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);" class=3D"">&gt; public without =
payment, it would be helpful to have a freely available =
</span></pre><pre style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; =
font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93; line-height: 21px; background-color: =
white; background-position: initial initial; background-repeat: initial =
initial;" class=3D""><span style=3D"font-size: 14px; font-family: Arial, =
sans-serif; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);" class=3D"">&gt; document (in =
English) from an authoritative source. Having such a </span></pre><pre =
style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=
=93; line-height: 21px; background-color: white; background-position: =
initial initial; background-repeat: initial initial;" class=3D""><span =
style=3D"font-size: 14px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(33, =
37, 41);" class=3D"">&gt; reference available would be helpful to the =
IETF community (and </span></pre><pre style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; =
font-size: 12pt; font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=93; line-height: 21px; =
background-color: white; background-position: initial initial; =
background-repeat: initial initial;" class=3D""><span style=3D"font-size: =
14px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);" =
class=3D"">&gt; researchers).</span></pre></div><div class=3D""><div =
style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: =E5=AE=8B=E4=BD=
=93; background-color: white;" class=3D""><span style=3D"font-size: =
14px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;" class=3D"">About the references =
to ISO documens, I think it is a general issue for IETF =
drafts.</span></div></div></div><div class=3D""><div class=3D""><p =
class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; font-size: 12pt; =
